s of it you should make sure  that the videos that you are choosing to  watch are actually from people that you  can trust or organizations that you can  trust Cordelia you spoke to some Tick  Tock users who you know used the  platform to search for information when  you spoke to them were they skeptical of  the kinds of information they found in  these videos or did they just take it at  face value  a lot of people really took things at  face value the people that I spoke to  often it just wasn't really a big  concern for them on the app these are  things that just seem like very everyday  low-risk kind of situations or at least  like they might seem like it because you  might not really feel the need to do any  additional leg work because it's like  while you're on these apps it feels like  you're talking to like a trusted friend  these are creators that you've followed  for extended period of time you probably  trust a lot more you just have to make  sure that you're aware of the fact that  not everything that you hear on Tick  Tock is right and you want to make sure  you're practicing your media literacy  skills to make sure you're getting the  best information also Tick Tock did  mention to me that when it comes to  verified check marks something to just  keep in mind is that that's meant to say  that this person is who they say they  are not necessarily that they are an  expert on whatever topic that they're  talking about  all right that's Cordelia James from our  personal Tech Team thanks for joining us  Cordelia thanks again Zoe  everything  man of the show please take a second to  leave a review and a five star rating it  helps other people find the show and  lets us know you like what we're doing  and if you want more Tech stories check  out our website wsj.com  I'm Zoe Thomas for The Wall Street  Journal thanks for listening  [Music]  foreign

